  "comments": "How the &quot;first letter &quot;E&quot; in &quot;BELGIQUE&quot; without central horizontal line&quot; for 1986 looks:<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5881e22b90c42.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5881e22b90c42.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"64\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nMint mark: Head of Archangel Michael, Koninklijke Munt van België - Monnaie Royal de Belgique, Brussels, Belgium<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Three main groups of Obverse are known</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Obverse</span><br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">I</span> - earlobe with curved outline.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">II</span> - earlobe with angled outline in fine line.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">III</span> - smaller earlobe with angled outline in thick line.<br />\r\nTogether with these features there are many more, some of which are marked by arrows in the following images.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Combinations</span><br />\r\n1986: <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">I</span>, <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">II</span>, <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">III</span>.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5f78c82a9a3e2.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5f78c82a9a3e2.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"198\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n1987: <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">II</span>, <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">III</span>.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6002065555350.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6002065555350.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"179\" height=\"249\" /></a>",
